#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119536 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119950 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce50e834-b8c1-56da-8750-241601cd1046" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Recursive Formula for a Geometric Sequence"}] :question/id #uuid "0a5038b8-1c2e-591c-9190-9493014fd98a" :question/math-academy-id "e-1506" :question/problem "What is the recursive formula for the following geometric sequence?\n\n$$\n1, \\: 4, \\: 16, \\: \\ldots\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The recursive formula for a geometric sequence with common ratio $r$ takes the form\n\n$$\na_{n+1} = r \\cdot a_{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the first term is $a_1={\\color{blue}1},$ and we can calculate the common ratio $r$ as\n\n$$\nr = \\dfrac{a_2}{a_1} = \\dfrac 4 1 = {\\color{red}4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the recursive formula is\n\n$$\na_{n+1} = {\\color{red}4} \\cdot a_{n} , \\qquad a_1 = {\\color{blue}1}, \\qquad n\\geq 1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119537 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119951 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6aee1b1d-3cb6-5f52-8973-13b067b1c41a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Term of a Geometric Sequence Given Its Recursive Formula"}] :question/id #uuid "25a92b77-314f-5e6a-8a26-5e631d10e4d0" :question/math-academy-id "e-1507" :question/problem "What is the $4$th term of the geometric sequence given below?\n\n$$\na_{n+1} = -3 a_n,\\qquad a_1 = 2,\\qquad n \\geq 1\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We use the recursive formula to compute the terms of the sequence up to the $4$th term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & =2 \\\\ {a}_{2} & =-3{a}_{1}=-3(2)=-6 \\\\ {a}_{3} & =-3{a}_{2}=-3(-6)=18 \\\\ {a}_{4} & =-3{a}_{3}=-3(18)=-54\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a_4 = -54.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119538 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119953 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "76437951-0d71-548b-b330-e494aa12c6a1" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Geometric Sequences"}] :question/id #uuid "33621cf4-4508-51d5-958b-18a6ec1ebc73" :question/math-academy-id "e-1508" :question/problem "Which of the three sequences below are geometric sequences?\n\nI. $10, \\: 20, \\: 30, \\: 40, \\: \\dots$\n\nII. $a_{n+1} = \\dfrac{1}{6}a_n,\\quad a_1 = 36,\\quad n\\geq 1$\n\nIII. $f(n+1) = 2f(n)-1,\\quad f(1) =2,\\quad  n\\geq 1$" :question/worked-solution "A sequence is geometric if there is a common ratio between its terms. Let's check each sequence in turn.\n\n- Sequence I is not geometric because not every pair of consecutive terms has the same ratio. To see this, we only need to go up to the third term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}}=\\frac{20}{10} & =2 \\\\ \\frac{{a}_{3}}{{a}_{2}}=\\frac{30}{20} & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Sequence II is a geometric sequence. The recursive rule $a_{n+1} = \\dfrac{1}{6}a_n$ tells us that each term is $\\dfrac{1}{6}$ times the previous term, so the common ratio is $r=\\dfrac{1}{6}.$\n\n- Sequence III is not a geometric sequence. To see this, we can calculate the first $3$ terms of the sequence and then compute the ratios of consecutive terms.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1) & =2 \\\\ f(2) & =2\\cdot f(1)-1=2\\cdot 2-1=3 \\\\ f(3) & =2\\cdot f(2)-1=2\\cdot 3-1=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe first two pairs of consecutive terms have different ratios:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{f(2)}{f(1)}=\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ \\frac{f(3)}{f(2)}=\\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn conclusion, only sequence II is a geometric sequence."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119584 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119952 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aae4cf92-f456-5b5f-bf92-1c4aed5ee4f6" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Term of a Geometric Sequence Given a Recursive Formula in Function Notation"}] :question/id #uuid "ae9a3613-9e84-53bd-ad35-48394adfdc30" :question/math-academy-id "e-4232" :question/problem "What is the $5$th term of the geometric sequence given below?\n\n$$\nf(n+1) = -5f(n),\\quad f(1) = -1,\\quad  n\\geq 1\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We use the recursive formula to compute the terms of the sequence up to the $4$th term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1) & =-1 \\\\ f(2) & =-5f(1)=-5(-1)=5 \\\\ f(3) & =-5f(2)=-5(5)=-25 \\\\ f(4) & =-5f(3)=-5(-25)=125 \\\\ f(5) & =-5f(4)=-5(125)=-625\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(5)=-625.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545822 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119950 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce50e834-b8c1-56da-8750-241601cd1046" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Recursive Formula for a Geometric Sequence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a6271c4-dc33-5178-8880-d84db8f789e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{1}{5}{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=5,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545374} {:answer/id #uuid "5fd17d56-55b0-5789-8b8e-7b8949679984" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}+\\frac{1}{5},\\,{a}_{1}=1,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545382} {:answer/id #uuid "6b8951a6-e073-51d8-932a-75d271fd5be2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}+5,\\,{a}_{1}=5,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545404} {:answer/id #uuid "6ed046c8-7602-5017-b313-39c70d6930b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=2,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545409} {:answer/id #uuid "e1e388cb-bd96-503a-915d-cbba5975a2c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=5{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=5,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545616}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5a6271c4-dc33-5178-8880-d84db8f789e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{1}{5}{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=5,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545374} :answer-field/id #uuid "256ce9ac-b6f2-58d9-9923-d36fccd40be2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545688}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5f82136c-d352-5849-8678-e3857b7e43c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-109803" :question/problem "What is the recursive formula for the following geometric sequence?\n\n$$\n5,\\,1,\\,\\frac{1}{5},\\,…\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The recursive formula for a geometric sequence with common ratio $r$ takes the form\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=r\\cdot {a}_{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the first term is ${a}_{1}=5,$ and we can calculate the common ratio $r$ as\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}}=\\frac{1}{5}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the recursive formula is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{1}{5}{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=5,\\,n\\ge 1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545829 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119950 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce50e834-b8c1-56da-8750-241601cd1046" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Recursive Formula for a Geometric Sequence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "59109616-a72d-56f4-b284-2356b9a3a252" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}-4,\\,{a}_{1}=7,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545370} {:answer/id #uuid "5e627b36-0bed-53c2-87b0-11792e481c81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=-4{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=3,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545380} {:answer/id #uuid "a09ab400-53e2-5d77-99dd-4639394319aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=-2{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=6,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545496} {:answer/id #uuid "cb91e927-0186-52d3-b60a-f7d417fe23d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=-\\frac{1}{4}{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=3,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545571} {:answer/id #uuid "f2a7e502-4c1c-5f69-ba12-c209563b85be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=-4,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545647}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e627b36-0bed-53c2-87b0-11792e481c81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=-4{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=3,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545380} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d7dfc4c-3be2-5c52-8f14-4925b82dc4d7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545728}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6e05b66e-ca2b-55a8-b1d5-5df4f7e7120d" :question/math-academy-id "q-109804" :question/problem "What is the recursive formula for the following geometric sequence?\n\n$$\n3,\\,-12,\\,48,\\,…\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The recursive formula for a geometric sequence with common ratio $r$ takes the form\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=r\\cdot {a}_{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the first term is ${a}_{1}=3,$ and we can calculate the common ratio $r$ as\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}}=\\frac{-12}{3}=-4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the recursive formula is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=-4{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=3,\\,n\\ge 1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545846 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119950 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce50e834-b8c1-56da-8750-241601cd1046" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Recursive Formula for a Geometric Sequence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e39963bd-2dfe-5a7e-adaa-2c2cf677ac70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}a_n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545621}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e39963bd-2dfe-5a7e-adaa-2c2cf677ac70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}a_n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545621} :answer-field/id #uuid "7685adc9-c06d-5b60-9d9b-882b9ed5af74" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545723} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "530993ed-b33b-597f-ad91-770ac1be6f70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545354}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "530993ed-b33b-597f-ad91-770ac1be6f70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545354} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9ff6506-1647-592e-b5f6-dfcf283ece96" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545770}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a5329a3e-b8b4-504e-8c17-47d6c0564352" :question/math-academy-id "q-249793" :question/problem "Consider the following geometric sequence:\n\n$$\n64,\\,32,\\,16,\\,…\n$$\n\nThe recursive formula for this geometric sequence is\n\n${a}_{n+1}=${{field-1}}$,\\,{a}_{1}=$\n{{field-2}}$,\\,n\\ge 1.$" :question/worked-solution "The recursive formula for a geometric sequence with common ratio $r$ takes the form\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=r\\cdot {a}_{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the first term is ${a}_{1}=64,$ and we can calculate the common ratio $r$ as\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}}=\\frac{32}{64}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the recursive formula is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=64,\\,n\\ge 1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545806 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119950 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce50e834-b8c1-56da-8750-241601cd1046" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Recursive Formula for a Geometric Sequence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2acc437e-a412-581d-8e81-dfe5cfc62ad9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545290}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2acc437e-a412-581d-8e81-dfe5cfc62ad9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545290} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f053b0a-afab-5b22-80de-3501f84a15e6" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545747} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6dc75461-f680-52f9-bdb9-64d7afe41e1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}{a}_{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545406}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6dc75461-f680-52f9-bdb9-64d7afe41e1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}{a}_{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545406} :answer-field/id #uuid "a57da2c0-90ed-5f07-addb-e7aacf7566d8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545749}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "225e6266-f488-590a-bcc1-b7110b1ab57c" :question/math-academy-id "q-249796" :question/problem "Consider the following geometric sequence:\n\n$$\n-48,\\,36,\\,-27,\\,…\n$$\n\nThe recursive formula for this geometric sequence is\n\n${a}_{n+1}=${{field-1}}$,\\,{a}_{1}=$\n{{field-2}}$,\\,n\\ge 1.$" :question/worked-solution "The recursive formula for a geometric sequence with common ratio $r$ takes the form\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=r\\cdot {a}_{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the first term is ${a}_{1}=-48,$ and we can calculate the common ratio $r$ as\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}}=\\frac{36}{-48}=-\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the recursive formula is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=-\\frac{3}{4}{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=-48,\\,n\\ge 1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545818 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119950 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce50e834-b8c1-56da-8750-241601cd1046" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Recursive Formula for a Geometric Sequence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d07ba6b-560e-5f76-bba4-ab3cc421726a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=-2{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{2}=24,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545222} {:answer/id #uuid "198dd29e-d1f9-5b83-b5d6-a3755e2179ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}-36,\\,{a}_{1}=24,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545250} {:answer/id #uuid "6f636481-d088-57f3-b4e1-1fff7ed219c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=24,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545410} {:answer/id #uuid "786b34ba-15b9-5365-b95c-9713f3204748" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=-2{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=24,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545427} {:answer/id #uuid "eabbcd8b-e3e1-568e-8bb4-7faa54e7eac9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=-\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=24,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545636}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eabbcd8b-e3e1-568e-8bb4-7faa54e7eac9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=-\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=24,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545636} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6960de4-32f2-5e23-a67e-c1fd22c3c7b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545778}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "498cc30d-95e0-5d5e-8baf-d608afabcdc8" :question/math-academy-id "q-44900" :question/problem "What is the recursive formula for the following geometric sequence?\n\n$$\n24,\\,-12,\\,6,\\,…\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The recursive formula for a geometric sequence with common ratio $r$ takes the form\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=r\\cdot {a}_{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the first term is ${a}_{1}=24,$ and we can calculate the common ratio $r$ as\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}}=\\frac{-12}{24}=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the recursive formula is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=-\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=24,\\,n\\ge 1.\n$$"}]}
